io Grande River and its tributaries including the South Fork\narea and along highway 160 to Wolf Creek Pass.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T11:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:43PM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample sub-tropical moisture will bring periods of moderate to\nheavy rain across the area from tonight into Friday morning\nbefore winding down Friday afternoon.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 6:49PM MDT until October 25 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte...Minor flooding\nis forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...From Friday morning to Sunday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 6.0 feet, Minor Flood. Considerable agricultural\nflooding occurs.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 5:45 PM MDT Thursday the stage was 4.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage\ntomorrow morning to a crest of 6.0 feet tomorrow evening. It will\nthen fall below flood stage Sunday morning.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.9\nfeet on 06/09/1985.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.153b5dda8f9373819ffabef65fe721dd445f03bd.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.153b5dda8f9373819ffabef65fe721dd445f03bd.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 6:41PM MDT until October 23 at 3:45AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Mineral County in south central Colorado...\nWestern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 345 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Rock falls are\noccuring in the steeper terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 639 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is already occurring in the warned area.\nBetween 1 and 3.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 2 inches are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWolf Creek Pass and the creeks and streams flowing into the San\nJuan River.\n- Highway 160 over Wolf Creek Pass is closed due to flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T03:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T05:28:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 230528 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1128 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains through the day Friday for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with areal stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Periods of moderate to heavy rain for the Continental Divide, tonight into early Friday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T06:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 220648 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1248 AM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-231300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T01:56:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... A Pacific storm system will track across the Great Basin and Four Corners regions through Friday, bringing moderate to heavy rainfall to the Continental Divide, with scattered showers and thunderstorms spreading across the rest of the district through early Friday morning. Another weather system will bring much cooler temperatures and widespread rainfall to all of the district start","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ctr01","station_name":"